iPhone Duo order wait times averaged 89 days despite falling by a week, according to <a href="https://www.ubs.com/global/en/investment-bank/insights-and-data/global-research/evidence-lab-overview.html">UBS Investment Bank</a> data as of October 30. (Via <em><a href="https://uk.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/ubs-reiterates-apple-stock-neutral-rating-on-iphone-wait-times-93CH-4945049">Investing.com</a></em>.) <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/hero_medium_2x-feature2.jpg" alt="" width="1466" height="825" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072526" /><br/>
The USB Evidence Lab tracker covers iPhone availability across more than 30 markets, and puts the iPhone Duo buyer wait time at nearly three months, even after the slight improvement.<br/>
<br/>
By comparison, iPhone 18 Pro wait times averaged around five days, down three days from the previous week, while the Pro Max held steady at roughly 18 days. UBS said reports of <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/23/iphone-duo-screen-cracks/">cracked screens</a> were unlikely to be the main reason for shorter Duo waits. But on their own, the figures don't tell us whether demand has weakened or supply has improved.<br/>
<br/>
iPhone Duo pre-orders <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/23/iphone-duo-apple-store-pickup-available-today/">slipped to late January</a> within minutes on the device's October 16 launch, but most people who queued on launch day walked away with a new phone. The reason, according to <a href="https://omny.fm/shows/power-on-with-mark-gurman/apple-embraces-a-touchscreen-macbook-iphone-duo-crackgate"><em>Bloomberg</em>'s Mark Gurman</a>, is that Apple allocated roughly 80% of its initial iPhone Duo inventory to its retail stores, with locations holding as few as 50 units each.<br/>
<br/>
At the time, Apple described demand as "nothing short of extraordinary" and said it was working to satisfy demand "as quickly as possible," so there's a good chance that, even if a delivery estimate for your order is way out in the future, it could improve over time.<br/>
